Package: cyclotraj
Title: Mixed-Model Testing of Treatment Effects on Longitudinal Count Trajectories
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Andrew", "Lakkis", email = "Andrew.Lakkis@pennmedicine.upenn.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A reusable framework for testing treatment-group differences in
    nested longitudinal count data: units measured repeatedly within subjects,
    where subjects are assigned to treatment groups and each observation is a
    count out of a sample-specific total. Counts are modeled with binomial
    generalized linear mixed-effects models (logit link) in two
    parameterizations of time that are read together: a continuous-time
    (linear-slope) model for sustained trends, and a difference-in-differences
    (categorical-time) model for timepoint-specific effects with no linearity
    assumption. Random intercepts for unit and subject handle the nested,
    repeated-measures structure. The package provides data preparation, model
    fitting, multi-degree-of-freedom joint Wald tests, multiplicity-controlled
    post-hoc contrasts on the log-odds scale that exponentiate to odds ratios,
    model diagnostics, figures with confidence bands, and tidy results tables. The motivating application is
    longitudinal T-cell clone tracking during cancer immunotherapy, but the
    method depends only on the data structure.
